WEBVTT

NOTE Unofficial English translation of the Thai narration. If it differs from the Thai original documents, the Thai original prevails.

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.690
The Senate Committee on
Agriculture and Cooperatives

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:10.280
held Meeting No. 38/2569 on
Monday, 9 November 2026.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:15.280
Mr. Sountorn Chaokijka, the committee
chair, presided over the meeting.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:21.040
First, the meeting considered progress
reports from the subcommittees.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:26.320
The committee's three current
subcommittees are chaired as follows.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.980
Livestock and Fisheries:
Mr. Ruchu Kaewlai.

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:36.320
Water Management in Farm Areas Outside
Irrigation Zones: Miss Amorn Sribunnak.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.740
And Integrated Agricultural
Networks: Mr. Choocheep Auekarn.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:46.080
The Integrated Agricultural
Networks subcommittee

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.978
reported progress on
its draft study report.

00:00:50.059 --> 00:00:54.433
The study aims to develop integrated
area-based management along

00:00:54.433 --> 00:00:58.397
the whole value chain, upstream,
midstream and downstream,

00:00:58.397 --> 00:01:02.293
raising the value of farm
products and access to markets.

00:01:02.374 --> 00:01:06.329
It found that the value
chain is not yet linked as a

00:01:06.329 --> 00:01:10.132
system, and agencies'
databases are not connected.

00:01:10.213 --> 00:01:13.811
Farmers get a small share of the
added value but carry much of

00:01:13.811 --> 00:01:17.119
the risk, and there is no
central coordinating mechanism.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:23.007
The subcommittee recommends setting
up an "integrated value-added

00:01:23.007 --> 00:01:27.443
agro-industrial zone" as a
central area linking production,

00:01:27.443 --> 00:01:31.578
grading, research, processing,
logistics and marketing.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:36.876
It would be managed at three
levels: state policy oversight,

00:01:36.876 --> 00:01:41.919
a zone board, and a zone office
offering one-stop service.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:47.815
The Water Management subcommittee
reported on its study

00:01:47.815 --> 00:01:51.998
visits on 29 to 30 October,
in three provinces.

00:01:52.079 --> 00:01:55.423
In Chai Nat, it studied
systems linking source water,

00:01:55.423 --> 00:01:58.073
water distribution,
and groundwater banks.

00:01:58.154 --> 00:02:01.755
In Suphan Buri, it found
dry-season shortages and

00:02:01.755 --> 00:02:05.724
high pumping costs, and
proposed surveying water needs

00:02:05.724 --> 00:02:08.958
and setting clear, fair
water-sharing rules.

00:02:09.039 --> 00:02:13.617
In Sing Buri, it studied managing
low-lying floodplains, and proposed

00:02:13.617 --> 00:02:17.532
helping people adapt their
livelihoods to water conditions.

00:02:17.613 --> 00:02:22.116
The key point: water sources must
be linked to distribution to meet

00:02:22.116 --> 00:02:26.619
farmers' needs, with local governments
and communities taking part.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:32.109
The Livestock and Fisheries
subcommittee is drafting a

00:02:32.109 --> 00:02:36.515
report on rabies prevention,
and reviewed an analysis

00:02:36.515 --> 00:02:40.838
of strengths, weaknesses,
threats and opportunities.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:44.245
Strengths: a national
policy, and agencies working

00:02:44.245 --> 00:02:46.839
together under the One Health approach.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:52.131
Weaknesses: the database is incomplete
and not yet linked across agencies.

00:02:52.211 --> 00:02:57.373
Threats include: only 30 percent of
local governments have animal control

00:02:57.373 --> 00:03:01.899
ordinances, and there are too few
veterinarians and field staff.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:05.844
Opportunities include working
with private firms or foundations

00:03:05.844 --> 00:03:08.359
on sterilisation, and
volunteer networks.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.820
The meeting also considered
two more matters.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:15.717
A request from the
senators-meet-the-people programme,

00:03:15.717 --> 00:03:18.615
lower southern group,
to support delaying

00:03:18.615 --> 00:03:21.725
the end of operations
of the Land Management

00:03:21.725 --> 00:03:24.906
Institute, a public
organisation, and to push

00:03:24.906 --> 00:03:27.875
for a royal decree
setting up a land bank.

00:03:27.959 --> 00:03:31.140
And the position of committee secretary.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:35.100
This summary is based on the
committee's press release.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:38.130
Meeting minutes and reports
are available through

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:40.899
the channels of the
Secretariat of the Senate.

